  "summary": "Health-tech M&A activity continues with Wildflower Health acquiring pelvic health platform Every Mother and Tempus AI announcing a $1.5 billion acquisition of genomic testing company Personalis, reflecting consolidation in specialized care and precision medicine. The competitive GLP-1 market saw legal action as Novo Nordisk sued Eli Lilly over allegedly deceptive advertising claims about drug efficacy. On the regulatory front, the Trump administration is deferring over $1 billion in Medicaid payments to California and Minnesota citing suspected fraud, while orphan drug manufacturers are lobbying for exemptions from new federal pilot programs aimed at cutting Medicare drug costs. Healthcare organizations are increasingly deploying AI-powered tools across clinical and administrative functions, though governance challenges remain around trust, resource constraints, and preventing misuse of these same technologies. Poland is accelerating its digital health infrastructure readiness and European Health Data Space adoption, while U.S. health systems are rethinking EHR ecosystems to better support telemedicine and point-of-care innovations. Separately, pharmaceutical companies are facing pressure on multiple fronts, including Agios Pharma discontinuing a sickle cell drug after disappointing Phase 2 data and broader concerns about post-pandemic policy directions affecting public health preparedness.",
